# Inline rename dismiss (mandatory)

Living spec: [`openspec/specs/ui/inline-rename/spec.md`](../../openspec/specs/ui/inline-rename/spec.md).
Rust contract + tests: [`crates/noviewlog-slint/src/rename_chrome.rs`](../../crates/noviewlog-slint/src/rename_chrome.rs).

## MUST dismiss

Any **pointer-down / click** outside the active rename `TextInput` ends rename
(commit if the draft is non-empty). Includes leftover sidebar stretch under
FILES/TERMINALS (`sidebar-dead-space` in `app.slint`). Empty FILES is **0px**
tall — the stretch **is** the empty area. Do **not** use a bare `Rectangle`
there.

Same on Linux and Windows. Do not add per-widget dismiss lists as the design;
keep the dead-space layer + real focus loss.

## MUST NOT dismiss

Mouse leave / `has-hover` false / pointer-move without a press.

Do **not** `self.focus()` on every blur (traps the editor).

## Tests

After changing rename or sidebar layout:

```
cargo test -p noviewlog-slint --lib
cargo test -p noviewlog-slint --test inline_rename_wiring
```
